{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Body Music Bass",
 "category": "Bass",
 "text": "Sound: the driving, machine-tight sequenced bass of 1980s body music (EBM): every sixteenth note a short, punchy pluck, jumping an octave on the off-beats.\n\nHow it's built: the Clock's 1/16 steps the Sequencer; its PITCH plays one oscillator whose saw and pulse are mixed, through the OTA filter; a short envelope snaps the filter open on every step (a click of brightness) while a second one holds the VCA open for the note. A touch of Drive at the end thickens it. MIDI In's PITCH into TRANSPOSE: hold a key around C3 and the line plays from it (until you do, it plays from C3).\n\nTweak: the filter's CUTOFF and RESONANCE while it runs; the envelope's DECAY (longer is rounder); the step knobs and on/off buttons; TEMPO (EBM sits around 115 to 130).",
